+# Changelog
+
+All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
+
+The format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).
+
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Added
+
+- **`budget` subcommand** — `tally budget --month YYYY-MM` prints each
+  configured category alongside its monthly spending limit and how much has
+  been spent so far. Each row is marked `ok`, `warn` (≥ 80 % of the limit),
+  or `over` (limit exceeded) so problem categories stand out at a glance.
+- **`CATEGORY_BUDGETS` and `BUDGET_WARN_RATIO` constants** in `tally/config.py`
+  — monthly USD limits per category and the warn threshold (default 0.80) that
+  controls when a row transitions from `ok` to `warn`.
+- **`budget_status()` in `tally/report.py`** — returns one row per budgeted
+  category with `spent`, `budget`, `ratio`, and `state` keys; drives the
+  `budget` command output and is independently testable.
